---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro'

const effectiveDate = 'October 4, 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Service & Licensing Information"
  description="ShorelineOps licensing, clinical responsibilities, service availability, and requirements for a separate facility agreement."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <div class="marketing-document relative py-16 sm:py-24 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Breadcrumb & Header -->
      <div class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-shoreline-500/10 border border-shoreline-500/20 text-shoreline-700 dark:text-shoreline-300 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-4">
          <Icon name="file-text" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
          <span>SERVICE & LICENSING INFORMATION</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">
          Service & Licensing Information
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Updated: {effectiveDate} · Product information; commercial terms require an executed agreement
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Key Guarantees Frosted Card -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-xl border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800/80 shadow-sm mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-bold font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mb-4">Core Principles & Facility Responsibilities</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <Icon name="shield-check" class="w-4 h-4 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Deterministic Safety</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">Available checks hold unresolved cases. Physical texture and clinical acceptance still require qualified review.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <Icon name="database" class="w-4 h-4 text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Data portability review</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">Confirm export coverage and controlled full-database recovery before facility rollout.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <Icon name="lock" class="w-4 h-4 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Resident data boundaries</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">Resident information must remain within facility-approved deployments and processing agreements.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Agreement Body -->
      <div class="space-y-10 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">01.</span>
            Open Core & Commercial Scope
          </h2>
          <p>ShorelineOps uses an open core model. Repository license terms govern use of the published software; paid hosting or commercial services require a separate agreement identifying the parties and accepted scope.</p>
          <p>This page is product information. It is not an executed Master Services Agreement, subscription contract, or BAA. Current clinical use requires a separate deployment and database for each facility.</p>
          <p>See the <a href="https://github.com/ShadowWalkerNC/ShorelineOps/blob/main/LICENSING.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="underline text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">repository licensing guidance</a> and applicable license files.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">02.</span>
            Clinical Care Responsibilities & Medical Disclaimer
          </h2>
          <p>Authorized facility clinicians retain responsibility for diet orders, ingredient assessment, fluid restrictions, and physical texture checks. ShorelineOps provides operational checks and holds unresolved cases; it does not establish that every clinical constraint or meal is safe.</p>
          <p>Validate current orders, recipe data, tray holds, and professional review procedures before clinical rollout. Never bypass NPO or allergen holds. Unavailable verification must remain on hold.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">03.</span>
            Proposed Subscriptions & Licensing
          </h2>
          <p>The pricing page describes the proposed community, Pro, and Enterprise offerings. Confirm actual availability, facility scope, provider access, billing methods, and accepted commercial terms before subscribing.</p>
          <p>Payment processing, cancellation periods, support commitments, and any offline license behavior must be documented in the executed agreement. No unattended purchasing or clinical authority is granted by a subscription tier.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">04.</span>
            Facility Data Ownership & Portability
          </h2>
          <p>Facilities must define data ownership, retention, authorized access, export, and termination procedures in the applicable agreement.</p>
          <p>The administrator export currently contains selected records; it is not a complete recoverable database image. Full-database backup and controlled restore must be tested separately. JSON, CSV, and SQLite exports are not interchangeable recovery guarantees.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">05.</span>
            Service Level Agreement (SLA) & Offline Resilience
          </h2>
          <p>Availability, support response times, recovery targets, and service credits require an executed agreement backed by deployment acceptance. No measured uptime guarantee is represented by this page.</p>
          <p>A local installation can operate without internet while devices remain connected to its application server. Disconnected tablets cannot confirm current clinical verification or saved actions, and guaranteed offline mutation replay is not available. Use an approved downtime and reconciliation procedure.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 6 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">06.</span>
            Contract Review
          </h2>
          <p>Commercial liability allocation and remedies must be reviewed by the contracting parties and stated in their executed agreement. This product information page does not establish a liability cap or replace legal review.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 7 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">07.</span>
            Agreement Responsibilities
          </h2>
          <p>Governing law and dispute procedures must be established in the applicable executed agreement. No jurisdiction is selected by this informational page.</p>

        </section>

        <!-- Section 8 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">08.</span>
            Contact & Legal Notices
          </h2>
          <p>Use the contacts identified in the applicable service agreement for formal notices. For product discussion, consult the <a href="https://github.com/ShadowWalkerNC/ShorelineOps" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="underline text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400">project repository</a>; do not submit resident information or credentials in public discussions.</p>

        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Action Navigation -->
      <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex flex-wrap gap-4 justify-between items-center text-xs">
        <a href="/privacy" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-shoreline-600 dark:text-shoreline-400 hover:underline font-semibold">
          <span>Read Privacy & Facility Responsibilities</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
        <a href="/security" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-900 dark:hover:text-white">
          <span>View Security & Deployment Responsibilities</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
